<small>Proposal review · 11 October 2026 · Contributor boundaries still to investigate</small>
<h1>A generic WYSIWYG editor for web components</h1>
<ol>
<li>Select a TypeScript file; contributors identify whether it defines a component and expose the relevant nodes.</li>
<li>Language and framework knowledge belongs to contributors, potentially TypeScript, HTML, CSS and Lit; the precise split still needs investigation.</li>
<li>The editor displays those nodes and connects UI actions to contributed operations.</li>
<li>No dependency on specific components, supported-name list, per-component adapter or mandatory editor metadata.</li>
<li>Phase 1 is selecting and seeing components through that shared path.</li>
<li>Sample-data setup and service substitution are deferred to phase 2; real-data access remains deferred.</li>
<li>Rendering errors replace the content inside Visual and Preview, keeping the tabs and controls available.</li>
<li>Use minimum size and zoom to fit through shared sizing and viewport capabilities.</li>
<li>Named components are examples for verification, never cases that receive custom support.</li>
<li>Revisit the investigation under these boundaries before deciding on implementation.</li>
</ol>
<p><small>The verbatim needs-analysis record is at .harness/design/existing-components-visual-needs-analysis.md. This corrected scope replaces the earlier factory/sample-data proposal; the earlier probes do not establish the contributor architecture required here.</small></p>
